# Spring Boot Service Conventions

## Package structure
```
com.learntrack.{service}/
  api/          REST controllers (thin — delegate to application layer)
  application/  Use cases / application services
  domain/       Entities, value objects, domain events
  infra/        JPA repositories, Kafka producers, outbox, external clients
  config/       Spring configuration classes
```

## Never publish to Kafka directly
Always write to the outbox table within the same DB transaction. Debezium handles delivery.

```java
// BAD
kafkaTemplate.send("profile.updated", event);

// GOOD — inside @Transactional
profileRepository.save(profile);
outboxRepository.save(new OutboxEvent(tenantId, "profile.updated", serialize(event)));
```

## Idempotency
All ingest endpoints must check the `Idempotency-Key` header before processing.

```java
if (ingestionJobRepository.existsByIdempotencyKey(idempotencyKey)) {
    return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of("status", "already_processed"));
}
```

## Structured logging with OpenTelemetry
Include `tenant_id`, `trace_id`, and event name in every log statement. Use SLF4J with MDC.

```java
MDC.put("tenant_id", tenantId);
MDC.put("event", "profile.updated");
log.info("Profile rebuilt for employee {}", employeeId);
```

## Error handling
Never swallow exceptions. Wrap infrastructure errors in domain exceptions and let the global `@ControllerAdvice` handle HTTP mapping.

## No `@Autowired` on fields
Use constructor injection only. This makes unit testing straightforward without Spring context.
